      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3905578110,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Loyalty.Member.Management/Application/Commands/HouseHoldAccountLinkingCommandHandler.cs",
      "line": 344,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3905578110",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "TriggerEmail swallows all exceptions and returns false without logging anything. That makes it hard to diagnose why email triggering failed (especially since the caller returns a controlled HoHEmailTriggerError). Consider logging at least the exception type here (without including PII such as email addresses) to align with other handlers in this service that log TriggerEmail failures.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Added typed logger injection to HouseHoldAccountLinkingCommandHandler and now logs the TriggerEmail failure operation plus exception type before returning the existing controlled failure. The log intentionally excludes exception messages and account, member, and email values to avoid exposing PII."
    }
  ],
